"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility, with initial findings suggesting a 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated October 10th) and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining on September 10th. The project has secured a $2M budget approved by the executive board. Current phases involve moving from design to development (led by Omar Jensen) and upcoming UI enhancements in October. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated effective January next year."
